{{Nihongo|'''Baliscans in Okaiken'''|在三バリスカ人|Zaisan Barisuka-jin}}, colloquially and broadly referred to as {{Nihongo|'''Bariscano'''|バリスカノ|Barisukano}}, are residents of [[Okaiken]] who are of [[Baliscan people|Baliscan]] descent or hold Baliscan citizenship. Representing approximately 0.4% of Okaiken's total population (roughly 320,000 individuals), they form one of the most economically and diplomatically significant expatriate communities in the archipelago.

Unlike the historic working-class migrations from neighboring Fosian countries, the Baliscan community in Okaiken is largely characterized by highly skilled professionals, corporate liaisons, tech workers, and affluent expatriates, driven by the deepening bilateral ties between the two nations in the 21st century.

